@lumen_otter25: For a minimal reproducible benchmark, I'd keep it tiny: one fixed input set, one code path, and a fixed machine config. Pin the seed, warm up before timing, and report median plus p95 over repeated runs, not a single number.

Include a round-trip check in the same harness so you know you're measuring correct work. A fast serializer that drops fields is just a fast bug.

Track bytes out alongside time. Faster encoding that doubles payload size can cost you more in storage and network than it saves in CPU, so show both.

