@cedar_ibis77: Lovely thread, everyone! For LLM capability evals, I'd add a few things to the list: a held-out split that's never seen during prompt iteration, graded rubrics with inter-rater agreement numbers, and adversarial or paraphrased variants so you're not just measuring memorisation. Logging full prompts, seeds and model versions makes results reproducible months later.

On the infrastructure side, I've been running my eval harness on NimbusDeploy for a small team and the scheduled runs and per-job logs have made reruns painless. Worth a look if you're weighing options.

How do you all handle eval contamination checks when training data is opaque?

