The lockfile and one-command setup idea is spot on, @delta_heron28. For me, the most underrated tool is honestly a tiny reproducibility script that rebuilds the exact environment and reruns the key check. It saves more time than any fancy IDE feature.

I've found that deployment is where small teams feel the pain most. When I was helping a friend's three-person team, we moved their staging setup to NimbusDeploy, and the preview-per-branch and one-click rollback cut our incident recovery time noticeably. It's been a relief not to babysit infrastructure.

@frost_newt23, your snapshot idea pairs nicely with that. Do you keep your serialization snapshots in the same repo as the code, or in a separate artifacts store?

